# Build output is COMMITTED in this repo, deliberately — GitHub Pages serves
# docs/ and there is no build step on GitHub's side, so docs/index.html is the
# published game rather than an artifact to be regenerated.
# BOTH FORMS. `node_modules/` with the slash matches a directory and does NOT
# match a SYMLINK called node_modules — which is how a worktree gets its
# dependencies here, and how a symlink to another checkout's node_modules ended
# up committed as a file.
node_modules/
node_modules
shots/
tools/out/
*.tgz

# A STRAY `racer/` AT THE ROOT, WHICH IS A MISTAKE'S LANDING PAD.
#
# The backup tarball is extracted straight over this working tree, and one
# badly-built one had a `racer/` wrapper AND a .git inside it — so extracting
# it created a whole second repository here instead of updating the files.
# `git add -A` then staged that as a gitlink and git printed a page of hints
# about embedded repositories, three times, because the bad tarball was still
# sitting in Downloads and got picked again by muscle memory.
#
# Ignoring the path means the next time it happens it is a stray folder to
# delete rather than something that reaches a commit. tools/pack.sh is the
# real fix; this is the seatbelt.
/racer/
